*Part of my [Build in Public](https://dev.to/zaerohell) series — sharing the real process of building SaaS projects from Playa del Carmen, México.*

*Repo: `zaerohell/iso27001-tablero` · 2026-10-17*

\#playadev #buildinpublic
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This is a submission for the &lt;a href="https://dev.to/challenges/hacktoberfest-week2-2026-10-12"&gt;Hacktoberfest Open-Source AI Challenge Week 2: Side Hustle&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


What I Built
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Independent e-commerce creators—especially Etsy artisans, Shopify boutique owners, and print-on-demand side hustlers—routinely suffer from the &lt;strong&gt;"Inventory Trap"&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;The Cost of Stockouts&lt;/strong&gt;: Missing sudden weekend demand surges because raw materials ran out, directly leaving revenue on the table and hurting marketplace search rankings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;The Curse of Dead Stock&lt;/strong&gt;: Over-ordering slow-moving catalog variants, tying up scarce working capital that should be funding marketing or new product launches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Large enterprises solve this with multimillion-dollar ERP systems like SAP or NetSuite, or expensive $300/month demand forecasting SaaS tools. Solopreneurs and side hustlers, on the other hand, are left guessing in Excel sheets or frantically reordering supplies after they've already sold out.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Restock-Predictor&lt;/strong&gt; is an AI-powered inventory intelligence micro-SaaS built specifically for these independent sellers. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Store owners simply drag and drop their historical sales export (columns: &lt;code&gt;Date&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;Item_ID&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;Quantity_Sold&lt;/code&gt;). Within two seconds, the platform:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyzes multi-item sales velocity, weekly cycles, and seasonal momentum.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Runs zero-shot tabular in-context regression via the &lt;strong&gt;TabPFN open-weight foundation model&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Computes both &lt;strong&gt;expected 30-day demand&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;probabilistic 90th-percentile safety stock buffers&lt;/strong&gt; to prevent stockouts during peak surges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generates an actionable, prioritized &lt;strong&gt;Purchase Order (PO) table&lt;/strong&gt; with one-click CSV export for suppliers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Logs every batch to &lt;strong&gt;MongoDB Atlas&lt;/strong&gt; for audit history and usage tracking.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Who Would Pay For It?
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Etsy makers and Shopify side hustlers generating \$2,000 to \$25,000/month in revenue. For an artisan maker, avoiding just &lt;strong&gt;one single stockout&lt;/strong&gt; on a high-margin weekend pays for an entire year of a \$15–\$25/month subscription.&lt;/p&gt;




