&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This is a submission for the &lt;a href="https://dev.to/challenges/hacktoberfest-week2-2026-10-12"&gt;Hacktoberfest Open-Source AI Challenge Week 2: Side Hustle&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


What I Built
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;FreelanceFlow AI&lt;/strong&gt; is a 100% local, privacy-first invoice and expense manager designed specifically for freelancers, solopreneurs, and independent contractors. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


The Problem
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;At the end of every month or tax season, freelancers face a painful chore: hunting down dozens of digital receipts and PDF invoices scattered across email inboxes and downloads folders (GitHub Copilot, Figma, AWS, Vercel, WeWork, Zoom, client dinners, and hardware purchases). Today, they have two frustrating choices:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;The Manual Spreadsheet Grind:&lt;/strong&gt; Manually typing invoice numbers, dates, tax amounts, and vendors into Excel or Google Sheets. It takes hours, leads to typos, and frequently causes missed tax write-offs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Expensive Cloud SaaS Apps:&lt;/strong&gt; Paying $20–$50/month for tools like Expensify, Dext, or QuickBooks that upload confidential financial documents, client names, and bank statements to proprietary cloud LLM APIs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Who Would Use &amp;amp; Pay for It?
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Freelancers and solopreneurs running lean side hustles who care deeply about:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Financial Data Confidentiality:&lt;/strong&gt; Keeping client billing records, NDAs, and receipts strictly on their own machines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Eliminating Recurring SaaS Fees:&lt;/strong&gt; Paying zero monthly AI token or subscription fees.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Tax Readiness:&lt;/strong&gt; Getting clean, categorized summaries and 1-click CSV exports ready for tax deductions and accountant handoffs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


Demo
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The app features a modern, responsive SaaS-style interface powered by Streamlit and Plotly:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;📊 Financial Health Dashboard:&lt;/strong&gt; 4 real-time KPI metric cards (Total Spend, Invoices Logged, Average Expense, and Top Category), plus interactive Plotly visualizations for monthly spending trends and category distribution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;📄 Smart Document Ingestion:&lt;/strong&gt; Drag-and-drop support for PDF invoices and receipt images (PNG, JPG, WEBP).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;🛡️ Instant Duplicate Detection:&lt;/strong&gt; Computes a cryptographic SHA-256 hash on upload and alerts you immediately if a document was already entered, preventing double deductions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;🤖 Gemma AI Extraction with Human-in-the-Loop:&lt;/strong&gt; Automatically parses Vendor, Invoice #, Date, Currency, Subtotal, Tax, Total, and Category into an editable confirmation form.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;💼 Full Expense Manager:&lt;/strong&gt; Filter by category, search by vendor/notes, adjust records in-place, and export clean CSVs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;🧪 1-Click Demo Mode:&lt;/strong&gt; Includes 12 pre-loaded fictional freelance expenses (Figma, GitHub, AWS, WeWork, Zoom, etc.) so judges can test every feature instantly without needing an active Ollama instance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A ready-to-test sample invoice (&lt;a href="https://github.com/snehalghadge59-blip/freelanceflow-ai/blob/main/sample_invoice.pdf" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&lt;code&gt;sample_invoice.pdf&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt;) is included in the repository.&lt;/p&gt;




